## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end security of hybrid AI platforms, spanning software supply chain and model governance, with practical incident response capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Secure software supply chain and model governance
- SBOMs, image/model signing, and cryptographic attestations
- Provenance verification and reproducible builds
- Policy-as-Code enforcement with OPA Gatekeeper
- Runtime attestation in Kubernetes environments
- Data provenance tracking for training datasets
- Incident response playbooks and success metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: sign an image with cosign
const { execSync } = require('child_process');

function signContainerImage(imageUrl) {
  // Generate SBOM
  execSync(`syft ${imageUrl} -o cyclonedx-json > sbom.json`);

  // Sign the image
  execSync(`cosign sign --key cosign.key ${imageUrl}`);

  // Attach SBOM as attestation
  execSync(`cosign attest --predicate sbom.json --type cyclonedx ${imageUrl}`);

  console.log(`Successfully signed ${imageUrl}`);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design concrete, layered security controls for a common integration risk in SaaS platforms. It tests understanding of both transport-layer and application-layer protections.

## Key Concepts
- Webhook signature verification using HMAC
- Replay protection via timestamps and narrow validation windows
- Secret management and rotation policies
- Transport security with mutual TLS (mTLS)

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');

function verifyWebhookSignature(payload, secret, signature, timestamp, windowMs = 300000) {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (now - timestamp > windowMs) return false;
  const data = \`${timestamp}.${payload}\`;
  const expected = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret).update(data).digest('hex');
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(signature), Buffer.from(expected));
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical containment and preventative controls for cross-account lateral movement in a real-world cloud environment.

## Key Concepts
- AWS account isolation, trust boundary hardening
- MFA, STS short TTLs, per-tenant KMS keys
- IAM Access Analyzer, SCPs, monitoring, and OPA-driven CI checks
- IR/DR framing with defined SLAs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple CI gate: reject policies granting "*" actions or resources
function isLeastPrivileged(policy) {
  const st = policy.Statement || [];
  for (const s of st) {
    const actions = Array.isArray(s.Action) ? s.Action : [s.Action];
    const resources = Array.isArray(s.Resource) ? s.Resource : [s.Resource];
    if (s.Effect === 'Allow' && (actions.includes('*') || resources.includes('*'))) {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

